<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Appendix A &#8211; Short Rezolve AI</h6>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Bonus Catalyst – We Believe a Russell 2000 Index Removal Could Be Very Likely</h2>



<p>Background &#8211; According to the former head of compliance at FTSE Russell, we, fuzzy panda research,<sup><a id="post-2661-footnote-ref-1" href="#post-2661-footnote-1">[1]</a></sup> were the very first investors to ever successfully use the FTSE-Russell Index appeals process to get a company REMOVED from the Russell 2000 index back in 2017.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>First Index Removal: WINS –37% in 2 days &amp; -99.9% total</strong></h3>



<p>Our first FTSE-Russell <a href="https://research.ftserussell.com/products/index-notices/home/getnotice?id=2586998">index appeal</a> was regarding <a href="https://seekingalpha.com/article/4059103-wins-finance-potential-sec-investigation-and-manipulation-of-a-russell-index#source=author_id%3A102078%7Cauthor_slug%3Afuzzy-panda%7Ccontent_type%3Aall%7Cfirst_level_url%3Aauthor%7Csection_asset%3Aprofile_page_author_analysis%7Csection%3Aprofile_page_author">Wins Finance (WINS</a>). Months of lobbying helped lead to FTSE-Russell created a new index rule regarding N-shares for Chinese companies listed in the USA. This rule immediately disqualified Wins Finance from being part of the Russell due to their fake US Headquarters. The result was that WINS fell 37% in the 2 days after the <a href="https://seekingalpha.com/article/4080251-wins-finance-index-removal-will-lead-to-heavy-forced-selling">index removal announcement</a> and the company has fallen 99.9% since.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Second Index Removal: LFIN –41.5% in 2 days &amp; -100% total </strong></h3>



<p>The next time we uncovered a false addition to the index involved <a href="https://www.cnbc.com/video/2017/12/18/small-cap-longfin-soars-2000-percent-after-acquiring-blockchain-company.html">Longfin Corp (LFIN)</a>. This time FTSE-Russell responded very quickly and within 2 weeks of our first contact with them Longfin Corp was <a href="https://research.ftserussell.com/products/index-notices/home/getnotice/?id=2588161">removed</a> from the Russell index. It fell 41.5% the day of removal and the stock is down 100% since.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="573" src="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/25-Longfin-Loses-Third-Value-After-Index-Removal-1024x573.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2725" style="width:585px" srcset="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/25-Longfin-Loses-Third-Value-After-Index-Removal-1024x573.jpg 1024w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/25-Longfin-Loses-Third-Value-After-Index-Removal-300x168.jpg 300w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/25-Longfin-Loses-Third-Value-After-Index-Removal-768x430.jpg 768w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/25-Longfin-Loses-Third-Value-After-Index-Removal-1536x859.jpg 1536w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/25-Longfin-Loses-Third-Value-After-Index-Removal.jpg 1788w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure></div>


<p>We similarly believe that Rezolve AI was an erroneous inclusion in the FTSE-Russell index. We have already reported the discrepancy and spoke to the FTSE Russell head of index compliance last week.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Rezolve Admits in Legal Documents to Trying to Dump Stock onto Index Funds</h3>



<p>What is even more shocking to us is that Rezolve has boldly admitted in their legal complaints that they filed that the company had planned to use the increased volume from a FTSE Russell index inclusion to dump shares onto the public. Essentially Dan Wagner and the company <s>stupidly </s>actually admitted in a legal complaint “under oath” that they had intended to rip off the FTSE-Russell index investors.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="555" src="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/26-Rezolve-Planned-to-Dump-Shares-onto-Index-Investors-1024x555.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2726" style="width:585px" srcset="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/26-Rezolve-Planned-to-Dump-Shares-onto-Index-Investors-1024x555.jpg 1024w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/26-Rezolve-Planned-to-Dump-Shares-onto-Index-Investors-300x163.jpg 300w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/26-Rezolve-Planned-to-Dump-Shares-onto-Index-Investors-768x416.jpg 768w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/26-Rezolve-Planned-to-Dump-Shares-onto-Index-Investors.jpg 1494w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><em>Source: <a href="https://iapps.courts.state.ny.us/webcivil/FCASeFiledDocsDetail?county_code=zEzqtsPq6F2XDrCec8Z3VQ%3D%3D&amp;txtIndexNo=9lF84hRDSE5n0ZOSIX0o5Q%3D%3D&amp;showMenu=no&amp;isPreRji=N&amp;civilCase=AYJrTf4RVQOS_PLUS_1NSsDz3%2Fg%3D%3D#:~:text=08/29/2025-,COMPLAINT,-%2D%2Dnone%2D%2D%C2%A0">Rezolve AI v. Yorkville Advisors et al, Complaint Filed Aug 29, 2025</a></em></figcaption></figure></div>


<p>FTSE-Russell’s inclusion and exclusions does not actually take into account things like company management teams, admitting to trying to rip off Russell investors, but maybe they would make an exception for the egregious Dan Wagner.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Index Analysis Shows Rezolve AI Could Be Removed from the Russell 2000 Immediately!</strong></h3>



<p>FTSE-Russell follows a rigorous <a href="https://www.lseg.com/content/dam/ftse-russell/en_us/documents/ground-rules/russell-us-indexes-construction-and-methodology.pdf">rules-based formula for inclusion</a>/exclusion, and we believe it was mistakenly misapplied (and potentially manipulated) which allowed this UK based AI company that IPO’ed with 0 IPO revenue to accidentally end up on US Indices.</p>



<p>FTSE-Russell 2000 index inclusion is a very formulaic process that’s simple and clear.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="328" src="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/27-Russell-2000-Criteria-Analysis-1024x328.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2727" style="width:585px" srcset="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/27-Russell-2000-Criteria-Analysis-1024x328.jpg 1024w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/27-Russell-2000-Criteria-Analysis-300x96.jpg 300w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/27-Russell-2000-Criteria-Analysis-768x246.jpg 768w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/27-Russell-2000-Criteria-Analysis-1536x493.jpg 1536w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/27-Russell-2000-Criteria-Analysis.jpg 1964w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure></div>


<p><strong>Step 1 = One Unique Country? = No Answer</strong></p>



<p>Step 1’s question is if the company is incorporated, headquartered, and traded in the same country?</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Rezolve AI &#8211; Country of domicile &#8211; UK</li>



<li>Rezolve AI &#8211; Country of incorporation &#8211; UK</li>



<li>Rezolve AI &#8211; Location traded – USA</li>
</ul>



<p>If all 3 answers are a yes and the same country, then a company can be included in that country&#8217;s indices. Since the answer is a No Rezolve Ai proceeds to a test based on assets &amp; revenue.</p>



<p><strong>Step 2 &#8211; Asset Test – Initially UK? But Now Canada (post GroupBy Acq) = No Answer</strong></p>



<p>Rezolve Ai IPO’ed with virtually no assets. It had little IP and only a small amount of cash listed in their FY 2024 20-F. Additional disclosure in the 20-F cites that Rezolve was keeping it’s cash in UK banks, but investor lawsuits also cited that RZLV’s CEO was attempting to move the company’s cash and BTC to Kazakhstan. This leaves ambiguity and makes the answer the Step 2 initially unclear. It probably was UK, but maybe it was Kazakhstan.</p>



<p>But after the acquisitions GroupBy and related party, BlueDot, an updated prospectus makes this Step 2’s answer more clear. &gt;75% of the Assets reported post the acquisition are NOT in the USA with <strong>63% of assets listed as being domiciled in Canada via BlueDot. </strong></p>



<p>Since Canada is not one of Rezolve’s first 3 answered HCI’s in Step 1 <strong>Step 2 is inconclusive. </strong></p>



<p><strong>Step 3 – Revenue test – 100% of IPO Revenue = Spanish Soccer Ticketing Revenue </strong></p>



<p>When the Index Inclusion test is run based on Revenue. If FTSE-Russell used the FY 2024 20-F it would shows that 100% of Rezolve’s FY 2024 &amp; FY 2023 reported revenue came from Spain&#8230;for soccer tickets.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="155" src="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/05-100-of-Revenue-Comes-From-Soccer-Ticket-Sales-in-Spain-1-1024x155.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2728" style="width:585px" srcset="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/05-100-of-Revenue-Comes-From-Soccer-Ticket-Sales-in-Spain-1-1024x155.jpg 1024w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/05-100-of-Revenue-Comes-From-Soccer-Ticket-Sales-in-Spain-1-300x46.jpg 300w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/05-100-of-Revenue-Comes-From-Soccer-Ticket-Sales-in-Spain-1-768x117.jpg 768w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/05-100-of-Revenue-Comes-From-Soccer-Ticket-Sales-in-Spain-1-1536x233.jpg 1536w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/05-100-of-Revenue-Comes-From-Soccer-Ticket-Sales-in-Spain-1.jpg 1594w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption"><em>Source: <a href="https://investor.rezolve.com/node/7701/html#:~:text=single%20source%20of%20revenue%20is%20for%20the%20commission%20from%20sales%20of%20football%20tickets%20for%20La%20Liga%20in%20Spain">Rezolve 20-F, Filed April 24, 2025</a></em></figcaption></figure></div>


<p>Spain is not one of Rezolve Ai’s primary HCI’s so the company would fail Step 3 and head to Step 4.</p>



<p><strong>Step 4 – Is the company HQ’ed in non-BDI Country? YES! United Kingdom. </strong></p>



<p>Finally at Step 4 of the country process FTSE-Russell should have reached a clear answer.</p>



<p>Rezolve Ai deserves to be tossed back across the pond to the United Kingdom.</p>



<p>Goodbye Wankers!</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>How we believe FTSE-Russell Could Have Mistakenly Included Rezolve in the Russell 2000?</strong></h3>



<p>We think that FTSE-Russell could have possibly been misled about the location of Rezolve’s revenue since the only disclosure in filings comes in an April 2025 20-F. The geographic disclosure of revenue only shows the revenue of GroupBy rather than the whole business. In this scenario, RZLV would’ve appeared to have ~52% of revenue in the USA.</p>



<p>However, that analysis would NOT include the actual core RZLV revenue of a mere $190k Spanish soccer tickets and it would also neglect to include the $2.5 million of Australian revenue from Bluedot. Including both of these numbers and revenue from the USA is &lt;50%. Which we believe should’ve placed RZLV as having a HCI of the UK.</p>



<p>Note &#8211; We think it would be ridiculous for FTSE-Russell to base it’s decision on unaudited pro-forma financials of a start-up acquired after the revenue was generated as their Russell 2000 index inclusion, so we hope that was not actually the reasoning. </p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="444" src="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/28-Russell-2000-USA-Revenue-Calculation-1024x444.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-2729" style="width:685px" srcset="https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/28-Russell-2000-USA-Revenue-Calculation-1024x444.jpg 1024w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/28-Russell-2000-USA-Revenue-Calculation-300x130.jpg 300w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/28-Russell-2000-USA-Revenue-Calculation-768x333.jpg 768w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/28-Russell-2000-USA-Revenue-Calculation-1536x665.jpg 1536w, https://fuzzypandaresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/28-Russell-2000-USA-Revenue-Calculation.jpg 1990w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure></div>


